From bde85d1ff5c18513d3ce3f86ac8dc2916ba2b342 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Claude (Sonnet)" <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 19:55:44 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(legal-kb): PostgreSQL store with DB-enforced temporal
 versioning (part 4B-1)

New module legal-kb-store (layer 2, depends only on legal-kb-schema):
- hand-written, checksummed, transactional migration in a dedicated
  schema (legal_kb) so drizzle-kit push never touches it
- DB-level constraints: EXCLUDE (gist) on half-open daterange for
  non-overlapping article versions, review consistency, hostile-char
  domains, label/FK/relation integrity, no cascading deletes
- insertCorpus: append-only, atomic, validated through loadCorpus
- readCorpus: consistent snapshot, re-validated through loadCorpus
- resolveCitation / versionsInForceAt in SQL, differential-tested
  against the pure engine (>4000 checks, all statuses observed)
- 130 new tests (real PostgreSQL, per-file throwaway schema); 55/55
  mutants killed (tooling/mutation/legal-kb-store.py)

All 378 previous tests are untouched. registry.ts, shared-types,
legal-kb-schema, src/db and package.json are unchanged.
Docs: task 0007, ADR-0004, handoff 0006, README, pitfalls, glossary.
